00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:50.860
something every contaminated site's professional encounters, heterogeneous subsurface conditions

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:57.360
that continually frustrate our conceptual site models. Imagine you arrive at a former industrial site

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.520
on the prairies. The phase two environmental site assessment reveals benzene concentrations

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:09.300
exceeding Alberta EPA tier one guidelines and one monitoring well, yet the adjacent well only eight

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:15.620
meters away shows no exceedance despite clear evidence of a historical release. This pattern is classic

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:21.540
in glacial till and outwash deposits where preferential pathways and low permeability lenses trap,

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:28.140
deflect or accelerate dissolved phase plumes in ways that uniform conceptual site models simply cannot

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:35.560
predict. Both British Columbia's contaminated sites regulation protocol for and CCME guidance are

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:40.600
clear that practitioners must characterize this heterogeneity through targeted sampling density

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:46.420
and high quality stratigraphic logging. Yet many regulatory submissions continue to rely on evenly

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:52.520
spaced monitoring grids that missed the dominant transport features entirely. Experience practitioners

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:58.760
instead prioritize high-resolution soil logging grain size analysis and hydraulic conductivity testing

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:04.720
at the faceyscale before they finalize plume boundaries or select remedies. They also insist on

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:11.080
multiple lines of evidence, soil vapor data, groundwater geochemistry and contaminant age dating,

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:16.820
rather than depending on a single monitoring event. The most common mistake I still see in the field

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:22.000
is the assumption that one or two representative samples adequately define the source zone or the

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.680
extent of the plume. That assumption routinely leads to under-designed remediation systems,

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:34.100
